## 📈 Risk Assessment Matrix

| Finding | Severity | Exploitability | Impact | Scope |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| SQL Backup | 🔴 Critical | Very Easy | Extreme | All staff & shareholders |
| Auth Bypass | 🔴 Critical | Very Easy | Extreme | All patients |
| Unencrypted PDFs | 🔴 Critical | Easy | Extreme | 3+ patients |
| FTP Exposure | 🟠 Medium | Moderate | Medium | Organizational |
| Mail Enum | 🟠 Medium | Easy | Medium | Phishing risk |
| No DNSSEC | 🟡 Low | Difficult | Low | DNS infrastructure |

---

## 📋 Recommendations (Priority Order)

### 🚨 Critical (24 hours)

1. Remove `/old/` directory from web root
2. Reset all staff credentials immediately
3. Disable patient portal until patched
4. Notify affected patients of potential breach
5. Engage legal/compliance teams

### ⚠️ High (1 week)

1. Fix authentication bypass in patient portal
2. Implement strong PDF encryption (AES-256)
3. Implement input validation on all forms
4. Enable HTTPS/TLS 1.2+ enforcement
5. Implement access control and audit logging

### 📌 Medium (1 month)

1. Migrate FTP to SFTP
2. Enable DNSSEC
3. Implement DMARC/DKIM/SPF
4. Deploy Web Application Firewall (WAF)
5. Conduct security awareness training

